The `type` getter of the abstract `Zone` class (src/zone.js:13-15) always throws — it never returns a value:

```js
get type() {
  throw new ZoneIsAbstractError();
}
```

`ZoneIsAbstractError` (src/errors.js:57-61) extends `LuxonError` (itself an `Error` subclass) with the message `"Zone is an abstract class"`. Every other abstract member (`name`, `universal`, `offsetName`, `formatOffset`, `offset`, `equals`, `isValid`) behaves the same way; concrete subclasses (IANAZone, FixedOffsetZone, InvalidZone, LocalZone) override them.
